# Normalise line endings.
#
# Git converts LF to CRLF on checkout under Windows by default, and two of
# these files stop working when it does. A Makefile with CRLF gives make a
# stray carriage return at the end of every recipe line, which it passes to
# the shell -- the error names a command that does not exist and looks
# nothing like a line-ending problem. A shell script with CRLF fails on its
# own shebang, reporting that /bin/sh is missing.
#
# So: LF everywhere, except the two file types Windows tools expect to find
# with CRLF.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.ps1  text eol=crlf
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf

# Binary, never touched.
*.jar    binary
*.zip    binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.png    binary
*.pdf    binary
